  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Above normal temperatures with mainly late week rain \nchances.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...High pressure both surface and aloft \noffshore will keep things warm and rain-free through Thursday...for \nthe most part. The exception may be some very spotty and very light \nWAA rain late Thursday over farthest inland zones and then again \nThursday night. Much better deep layer for ascent comes Friday with \na cold front and height falls/PVA from a deep trough developing \nunder a Great Lakes cutoff low. Available moisture doesn't quite \nlook as scant as compared to yesterday especially inland so our QPF \nis a bit higher there but still generally capped at 0.25\".",
